    "wgmma_probe": {
      "note": "Phase 0 of docs/kernels.md Part 3: the hand-written WGMMA ceiling probe of dev/kernels/wgmma_probe.cu. One warpgroup issues wgmma.mma_async.sync.aligned.m64n128k16.f32.bf16.bf16 from a resident shared-memory tile, through a hand-built descriptor in the interleaved K-major form, with no global memory traffic in the timed loop. The 1block row is one warpgroup on one SM; the grid row is two warpgroups on every SM of the card. fraction_of_peak is the rate over the card's declared bf16 peak of 989 TFLOP/s (backends/cuda/caps.json), and fraction_of_sm_share is the 1block rate over the per-SM share of that peak, 989 over 132, or 7.4924 TFLOP/s. Passes are four atoms each, so one pass is 1048576 flop. The correctness row is the sum of the 8192 accumulators against a host reference over the same input; a descriptor that reads the wrong tile fails it, because the two operands differ. The probe needs sm_90a, which no device configuration of .bazelrc emits, so the card job builds it inside the container with the tree's builder before it runs it.",
      "device": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3 (sm_90a)",
      "validated_on": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3 (sm_90a)",
      "precision": "bf16",
      "measurement": "modal run tools/modal/app.py::card_job --name wgmma_probe",
      "origin": "docs/kernels.md Part 3 phase 0, dev/kernels/wgmma_probe.cu, dev/kernels/README.md",
